## Steps to Create Sales_Forecast.pbix:
Connect to Processed Data:

## Open Power BI Desktop.
Click on "Home" > "Get Data" > "Text/CSV" and load the sales_data_cleaned.csv file from the data/processed/ folder.
Create Visualizations:

## Sales Over Time: Create a line chart to display sales trends over time. Use date as the x-axis and sales as the y-axis.
## Region-Wise Sales: Use a bar chart to show total sales per region. Use region as the x-axis and total sales as the y-axis.
## Top Products: Create a table to display top-selling products based on total sales and product_id.
## Inventory vs. Sales: Use a scatter plot to analyze the relationship between inventory and sales.
## Filters and Slicers:

Add slicers for store_id, region, and date to allow dynamic filtering.
## Save File:

Save the dashboard as Sales_Forecast.pbix in the dashboards/ folder.
